7-Zip 26.05 legacy port - License
=================================

This repository is a legacy port of 7-Zip to old Windows and DOS platforms.
It is free software and is distributed under the same terms as 7-Zip itself,
primarily the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your
option) any later version (GNU LGPL-2.1-or-later).


Copyright
---------

  7-Zip                     Copyright (C) 1999-2026 Igor Pavlov
  Legacy port (this work)   Copyright (C) 2026 ages2001

7-Zip was created by Igor Pavlov. This port adapts 7-Zip 26.05 to Windows
3.0/3.1x, Windows NT 3.1-4.0 / 2000 / XP(x64), Windows 9x, Win32s and DOS; it
adds native 16-bit Windows and DOS front ends and the platform installers. All
original 7-Zip copyright and license notices are preserved in the source files.


License terms
-------------

The license structure is inherited from 7-Zip and is unchanged:

  - Most source files are under the GNU LGPL.
  - CPP/7zip/Compress/Rar* (RAR decoding) is under the GNU LGPL with the
    "unRAR license restriction": you must follow both the GNU LGPL and the
    unRAR restriction (the RAR code may not be used to recreate the RAR
    compression algorithm).
  - A few decoders are under BSD licenses (LZFSE/ZSTD: BSD 3-clause,
    Copyright Apple Inc. and Facebook Inc.; XXH64: BSD 2-clause).
  - Some files are in the public domain where stated in the file.

The additions made by this port (the native 16-bit Windows/DOS front ends, the
Win16/DOS/NT/Win32s adapters and the installers under src/Compat) are released
under the GNU LGPL-2.1-or-later, so the project as a whole remains LGPL-
compliant.

The complete, authoritative 7-Zip license text is included in this repository
as `LICENSE-7zip.txt` (a verbatim copy of 7-Zip's own `src/DOC/License.txt`).
The full text of the GNU LGPL is available at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/ .


